Thanks @nicolas-grekas , added it as `testInvalidateTagsWithHashTagInPrefix()` in `RedisTagAwareClusterAdapterTest`, pretty much as you wrote it.

And yeah, it catches exactly that case. With the prefix set to `{app}:` the old temporary key landed in a different slot than the tag set, so `SUNIONSTORE` went cross-slot and `invalidateTags()` quietly returned `false`. Pinning the temp key to the same slot with `{prefix+id}id` is what makes it pass now.
